# Authentication

This template does not ship auth. Identity is a method argument. The shipped notes
service takes `UserDetails` from `Depends(get_user_details)`. A later bearer-token
check builds that object, or the fields the method already takes. Do not put a
credential on a service `__init__`. Do not import `Request` in `services/`. Do not
authenticate a remote MCP call with a session id or a cookie.

Construct the verifier in `lifecycle/` only. No module-level security scheme or
client. Pin signing algorithms, check audience and issuer, and do not log the
token. A token for this server must not be accepted for another resource, and its
scopes must match the tool.

Probes and `GET /metrics` do not perform that check. If you later need a uniform
pre-route 401, register ASGI only in `_add_middlewares_in_order`, before
`CorrelationIdMiddleware`, exempt paths via `app_consts.py`, and talk to a
service — never a client. The root README Authentication section says the same
thing, as do `src/app/state/README.md` and `src/app/middlewares/README.md`.
